# Fourier Series Visualizer

Interactive visualization tool for Fourier series decomposition, built in Python.

Developed alongside ENGR 311 — Transform Calculus and Partial Differential Equations at Concordia University.

## What it does

- Visualizes Fourier series approximations for square, sawtooth, and triangle waves
- Real-time harmonic decomposition with interactive slider (1 to 50 terms)
- Frequency spectrum showing harmonic coefficients
- Approximation error plot with RMS value
- Convergence analysis — RMS error vs number of terms

## Why it matters

Fourier analysis is fundamental to aerospace engineering — used in vibration analysis, signal processing, structural dynamics, and control systems. This tool makes the math visual and interactive.

## How to run

```bash
pip install matplotlib numpy
python fourier_visualizer.py
```

## Controls

- **Slider** — adjust number of harmonic terms (N)
- **Square / Sawtooth / Triangle buttons** — switch between wave types

## Tools

Python, NumPy, Matplotlib

## Skills demonstrated

Numerical methods, frequency domain analysis, signal decomposition, Python programming, engineering visualization
